# The cases that the SQL function effective_grants(bot_id) and the C# rule GrantRules.Effective must agree on.
# Both test projects read this file; there is no second copy.
#
# One case per line:  name | grants along the path, the bot first and the root last | expected effective grant | flags
#   - The optional last field is a flag. no-own-row means the bot's own closure row (distance 0) is missing, which hides every tool.
#   - A grant is none (the bot has no grant row), deny, ask, or allow. Add :review for a grant that needs review.
#   - The expected value is none, deny, ask, or allow. none means the tool is invisible to the bot.
#   - The depth is the number of grants listed: one is a root bot, four is a bot three levels below the root.

# No grant, and each plain grant, on a root bot
no grant at the root                          | none                         | none
deny at the root                              | deny                         | deny
ask at the root                               | ask                          | ask
allow at the root                             | allow                        | allow

# Depth 1: a bot and its parent
allow under an allow parent                   | allow,allow                  | allow
allow under an ask parent                     | allow,ask                    | ask
allow under a deny parent                     | allow,deny                   | deny
ask under an allow parent                     | ask,allow                    | ask
deny under an allow parent                    | deny,allow                   | deny

# Depth 2
allow all the way up, depth 2                 | allow,allow,allow            | allow
grandparent asks                              | allow,allow,ask              | ask
grandparent denies                            | allow,allow,deny             | deny
parent denies                                 | allow,deny,allow             | deny
the bot asks, ancestors allow                 | ask,allow,allow              | ask

# Depth 3
allow all the way up, depth 3                 | allow,allow,allow,allow      | allow
the root asks                                 | allow,allow,allow,ask        | ask
the root denies                               | allow,allow,allow,deny       | deny
ask all the way, the root denies              | ask,ask,ask,deny             | deny

# A missing grant anywhere on the path hides the tool
the parent has no grant                       | allow,none                   | none
the grandparent has no grant                  | allow,allow,none             | none
the root has no grant, depth 3                | allow,allow,allow,none       | none
a missing ancestor in the middle              | allow,none,allow             | none
the bot has no grant, ancestors allow         | none,allow,allow             | none

# A bot missing from its own closure table is not in the tree, so it is granted nothing
the bot has no closure row of its own         | allow,allow                  | none | no-own-row

# A grant that needs review counts as ask, and never as more
needs review, allow                           | allow:review                 | ask
needs review, ask                             | ask:review                   | ask
needs review, deny                            | deny:review                  | deny
needs review in the parent                    | allow,allow:review           | ask
needs review in the root, depth 3             | allow,allow,allow,allow:review | ask
needs review in the bot, parent denies        | allow:review,deny            | deny
needs review in the parent, the bot asks      | ask,allow:review             | ask
needs review and a missing ancestor           | allow:review,none            | none
